--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB PARITY — reproduced VERBATIM from web/src/components/data-display/UserCell.tsx
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Empty detection (em-dash) : !user || (!user.name && !user.email && !user.id)
                              (untrimmed truthiness — a whitespace-only name is "present").
  Display-name priority     : name?.trim() || email.split('@')[0] || id || t('avatar.unknown').
                              Each || short-circuits on a NON-empty string, so "@host" (empty
                              local-part) falls through to id / "Unknown user".
  Avatar initials (web      : split on whitespace → first letter of first two words; single word
   avatarInitials)            → first two chars; empty/whitespace → "?".
  Email line                : shown beneath the name only when showEmail && email present.
  Sizes (web SIZE_PX)       : xs=16 sm=24 md=32 lg=48 (default sm).
  i18n key from source      : avatar.unknown → "Unknown user"  (present in UserCell.strings).

  States mapping (the web cell is a synchronous presentational cell with two branches —
  em-dash empty and populated; the P4 surface binds it to the P1/S8 state holder and renders
  the full leaf-contract state set): loading→skeleton row; empty→the web em-dash; error→
  compact error + Retry; content→populated cell (a resolved-but-blank identity still projects
  isEmpty → em-dash, faithful to web); stale/offline→cached cell + freshness indicator.

